==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*peh₁-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|penaunce}}, from {{der|en|xno|-}}, from {{der|en|fro|peneance}}, from {{der|en|la|paenitentia||penitence}}. {{doublet|en|penitence}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpɛn.əns/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-penance.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{hyph|en|pen|ance}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A voluntary self-imposed [[punishment]] for a [[sinful]] act or wrongdoing. It may be intended to serve as [[reparation]] for the act.
#* {{RQ:Coleridge Ancient Mariner}}
#*: Quoth he, "The man hath '''penance''' done, / And penance more will do."
# A [[sacrament]] in some Christian churches.
# Any instrument of self-punishment.
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[repentance]]
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[pain]]; [[sorrow]]; [[suffering]]
#* {{RQ:Chaucer Troilus|book=IV}}
#*: ne Joy nor '''penance''' he feeleth none.

====Synonyms====
